---
title: Passeridae
---
# Passeridae

Passeridae is the Old World sparrow family, small, thick-billed seed-eaters
closely associated with human settlement. Most species build an untidy domed
nest of grass and straw crammed into a cavity, a creeper or the base of a larger
bird's stick nest. They are gregarious throughout the year and will nest in
loose colonies where sites allow. See [[house-sparrow]].
